<h2>Destruction</h2>
<p>Author fracture on ordinary prefabs. Native Blast/Jolt handles impacts and connected fragments.</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>Fracture3D</code> on mesh children describes how a mesh splits.</li>
  <li><code>Masonry3D</code> describes repeated brickwork with material density.</li>
  <li><code>Destructible3D</code> owns the assembly and runtime splitting.</li>
  <li><code>FractureDebris3D</code> covers cosmetic debris cleanup.</li>
</ul>
<pre><code>local Destruction = require("demi.physics.destruction3d")

local accepted, error, affected = Destruction.impact({
    entity = id, position = {x = x, y = y, z = z},
    radius = 0.5, energy = 200, impulse = 20,
})
Destruction.damage_part(id, part, amount)

local state = Destruction.state(id)
-- status, error, revision, bodies, and part-to-entity mappings

local checkpoint, error = Destruction.checkpoint(id)
-- Restore on a fresh attached assembly; queued changes must have committed.
if checkpoint then Destruction.restore(fresh_id, checkpoint) end
Destruction.retire_debris(id) -- retire detached physical groups</code></pre>
<p>Optional gameplay packages add weapons and proximity streaming. Runnable labs: <code>destruction_3d_lab</code>, <code>destruction_weapons_3d_lab</code>, <code>fracture_prefab_lab</code>.</p>

<h2>Transforms</h2>
<pre><code>local T = require("demi.transform3d")
local x, y, z = T.get_position(id)     -- local-space scalars
T.set_rotation(id, rx, ry, rz)         -- Euler radians
T.set_scale(id, sx, sy, sz)
local fx, fy, fz = T.forward(id)       -- world-space unit vector
T.look_at(id, tx, ty, tz)              -- aim at a world point</code></pre>
<p>Getters return separate numbers and <code>nil</code> per coordinate when the entity or component is missing.</p>
